---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Now" description="October 2026: building Hydra and working out how to do good work with AI.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Now</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated: 14 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      This is my <a href="https://nownownow.com/about" target="_blank">now page</a>,
      a snapshot of what I'm focused on at this point in my life.
    </p>

    <h2>Making</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="https://usehydra.co.za" target="_blank">Hydra</a> is my main focus.
      I'm working on customer retention for South African businesses, with a lot
      of attention going into the experience of joining through WhatsApp and
      the tools a merchant needs to run things. There are plenty of moving parts,
      so I'm trying to keep each piece small enough to understand and finish properly.
    </p>

    <h2>Figuring out</h2>
    <p>
      How to work well with AI whilst staying involved in the decisions.
      I'm spending time breaking work into smaller features, checking each one,
      and being more deliberate about which model needs to do what. It's very
      easy to produce more work than you have time to properly look at.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <p>
      Catching up on the lessons sitting inside these projects. My thoughts on
      AI have moved on since <a href="/writing/2025-01-03-thoughts-on-coding-with-ai/">early 2025</a>,
      and the ideas in <a href="/writing/taste/">Taste</a> have become a lot more
      practical whilst building Hydra. There is quite a bit to unpack.
    </p>

    <hr />

    <p>
      <em>
        Inspired by <a href="https://sive.rs/now" target="_blank">Derek Sivers</a>
        and the /now page movement.
      </em>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .last-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
</style>
